{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver's arrival is established on two independent carriers: the trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 2026-09-18T19:11:48, and the GPS trace's first qualifying in-geofence fix is timestamped at the very same second, with a dwell-start offset of 0.0 s against the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius. POL-NS-01(a) and limb (b), read with the POL-NS-02 proximity test, are therefore both made out, and the trace supporting them is COMPLETE at weight 1.0 with 100% coverage and no gaps.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02748", "EV-GPS-02748"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.first_ts",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver held position inside the pickup geofence for a continuous 200 seconds - 21 consecutive qualifying fixes from 19:11:48 to 19:15:08 - which exceeds the 180-second free waiting period in force for this trip under platform_policy.free_wait_sec; the derived shortfall_sec is -20.0, that is, no shortfall. POL-NS-01(c) is satisfied, and because the dwell is not shorter than the free waiting period the premature-cancellation refund route in POL-NS-06 is not engaged. The record sets no longer no_show_threshold_sec, so no additional threshold applies to the cancellation in limb (d).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02748", "EV-TRIP-02748"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This is not a false-arrival case under POL-NS-05. At the marker timestamp the trace's first qualifying in-geofence fix is at 19:11:48, inside the 50 m radius, so the 'I'm Here' tap was not pressed from more than 300 m away, and the driver's nearest approach to the pin across the trace is 0.44 m; the driver was stationary at the pickup, not travelling at 15 km/h or more. The arrival marker therefore validly started the waiting clock, and no false-arrival event should be recorded against the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02748", "EV-TRIP-02748"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.dwell_start_offset_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The termination was not an abandonment of the pickup. The chat log shows the driver opened contact 30 seconds after arriving ('cannot find you, where are you', 19:12:18), the rider answered 'at the lift lobby' at 19:12:48, and the driver then held position for a further 142 seconds, terminating only at 19:15:10 after the full free waiting period had been served. The rider's own track records 40 fixes all at 0.0 km/h across the window, so nothing in the admissible trace shows the rider moving towards the vehicle before termination.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02748", "EV-GPS-02748"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.distinct_speeds_kph",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The cancelled trip's money is internally sound: EV-FARE-02748 carries a cancellation-fee line of SGD 4.50, equal to platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd (4.50) and to fee_schedule.defaults (4.50), so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect and no fare-integrity ground on which to discount this dispute. The contested amount is SGD 4.50 and the fare breakdown shows it charged with refund_issued_sgd of 0.00.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02748", "EV-TRIP-02748"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No POL-NS-09 limb is engaged and there is no basis to hold the fee or send this trip to human review. The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the absolute count of 4, and 1 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d (137) is 0.007, below the 0.08 rate - both limbs are required and neither holds. rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d are both 0, so the repeat-dispute trigger is absent. The trip record and the GPS trace agree on arrival, dwell and rider presence rather than contradicting each other, and the only impaired artifact in the bundle is EV-ADVIS-02748-01, MISSING under issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT at weight 0.0, which carries no deciding fact and on which no driver claim relies.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02748", "EV-RPROF-02748", "EV-ADVIS-02748-01", "EV-TRIP-02748", "EV-GPS-02748"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver does not press the fee and does not claim compensation. The trip was terminated under cancellation_reason_code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, and POL-NS-01(d) states in terms that this code does not satisfy limb (d), so the no-show fee is not chargeable under POL-NS-01 on this record and no POL-NS-07 payout is asserted. What the same limb (d) sentence supports is that the mis-selected reason code is a driver-education referral and nothing more: on the facts above the driver truly arrived, truly waited the 200 seconds required, and the 4.50 fee line reconciles, so the ruling should be confined to recording the code mis-selection as that referral, with no false-arrival finding, no fare-integrity defect and no escalation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02748", "EV-GPS-02748"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-07"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.5,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-01: driver-education — the trip was terminated under cancellation_reason_code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, which does not satisfy POL-NS-01(d); a no-show fee is chargeable only where the driver records RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT. The driver's stationary fixes lay inside the arrival radius and the fee is refunded, so the mis-selected code is recorded for driver education only."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "The SGD 4.50 no-show fee charged on TRP-02748 is refunded to the rider in full, with no payment to the driver. POL-NS-01 makes a no-show fee chargeable only if all four of its conditions hold, and limb (d) fails on the face of the record: the trip was terminated by the driver at 19:15:10 under cancellation_reason_code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE (EV-TRIP-02748), and POL-NS-01(d) states in terms that this code is the driver's own admission that he could not find the rider and does not satisfy limb (d). The recognised codes are RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE and EXCESSIVE_WAIT.\n\nBoth advocates concede this, and the driver's remaining points are accepted but do not change the outcome. The driver did arrive and did wait: on EV-GPS-02748 (COMPLETE, weight 1.0, 100% coverage, no gaps) the first qualifying in-geofence fix is at 19:11:48 — the same second as the 'I'm Here' tap on EV-TRIP-02748 — inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, and he held position for a continuous 200 seconds across 21 qualifying fixes to 19:15:08, 20 seconds beyond the 180-second free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec). So POL-NS-01(a)-(c) hold and the arrival marker is not false: the driver was inside the radius, not more than 300 m away and not travelling at 15 km/h or more, so no POL-NS-05 false-arrival event is recorded. The money reconciles: the SGD 4.50 cancellation line on EV-FARE-02748 equals platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd and fee_schedule.defaults, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect.\n\nBecause the driver's stationary fixes lie INSIDE the arrival radius and the code is DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, POL-NS-01 itself resolves the case for the rider — the fee is not chargeable, the ruling is FULL_REFUND of the SGD 4.50 with no driver compensation, and the mis-selected code is recorded as a driver-education referral. The rider's own evidence runs the same way: POL-NS-04 is made out on all three limbs — (a) the rider sent the locating message 'at the lift lobby' at 19:12:48 inside the waiting window; (b) the driver posted no reply within 120 seconds of it and made no in-app call before cancelling at 19:15:10; (c) the rider's track stayed inside the 100 m STANDARD presence radius for 40 of 40 qualifying fixes (maximum 19.67 m).\n\nNo escalation. EV-TRIP-02748, EV-GPS-02748, EV-CHAT-02748 and EV-FARE-02748 are each COMPLETE at weight 1.0; the trace has no gaps and the chat sequence and message count are intact, so no POL-NS-08(a)-(d) impairment exists and POL-NS-09(a)-(e) does not fire. The only impaired artifact is EV-ADVIS-02748-01, MISSING (issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT) at weight 0.0; it carries no deciding fact and neither side rests a ground on it. Confidence is 0.95, below the cap of 1.0 set by the minimum weight of the artifacts carrying the deciding facts. The monetary effect (SGD 4.50) is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "No traffic advisory covers this pickup: EV-ADVIS-02748-01 is MISSING and carries weight 0.0, an absence that is itself citable. Under POL-NS-06 the only route by which a driver's separate in-geofence intervals could be summed toward the waiting period requires a traffic_advisory that is present and populated, so there is nothing on this record that could be used to extend or excuse the waiting clock on the driver's side.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02748-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
